I just finished my priest quest over the long weekend.  He went from
experience level 15 to 30 as a result of eating so many wraiths.  I
dealt with the monsters by going up and down the stairs a lot, this way
I could finish off not more than 8 monsters, then rest up for the next
batch.  The mitre of holiness was a big disappointment after the the
tsurugi of muramasa.

The thing that really had me worried was running out of food.  I started
out with 4 or 5 rations, but it takes thousands of turns to kill all
those monsters.  I wasn't sure how my god would feel about the
unfortunate death of the priest of Moloch, so I hesitated to pray, and
the wraiths didn't seem to have many calories.  None of those undead
monsters is good eating.

When I reached the level of whats-his-name, he followed me back up the
stairs, sparing me the chore of fighting through all the monsters on the
bottom level (not to mention traps).  It was kind of amusing.  I kept 
zapping him away with a wand of teleport and he kept teleporting right
back again.



